                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "ragdolled"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0c462318-261f-3131-a6c3-42266722224e",
                        "entry_id": "026b1199-4c6a-38b8-a35a-037c1068203e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be flung about so that the limbs move loosely."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1de11ba2-678a-3fcb-9a5c-2e0d8c62144b",
                        "entry_id": "026b1199-4c6a-38b8-a35a-037c1068203e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To move, roll, fall, etc., so that the limbs move loosely."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d241a6a8-8ae6-464d-bade-2104d7421f05",
                                "sense_id": "1de11ba2-678a-3fcb-9a5c-2e0d8c62144b",
                                "text": "I was so tired that potholes, fumes and noise aside, I slept regardless, my head rag-dolling from side to side."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6091919b-da9b-3c29-affa-f5d16a78ecd5",
                        "entry_id": "026b1199-4c6a-38b8-a35a-037c1068203e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To fling about so that the limbs move loosely."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d74109db-051c-4e3b-b24f-1c91149a0529",
                                "sense_id": "6091919b-da9b-3c29-affa-f5d16a78ecd5",
                                "text": "“Manhandle” isn’t the term for what he’s doing. It’s something more desperate, the way he’s clutching and yanking and pawing at him—our guy is ragdoll'''ing his antagonist."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bce157d0-e12f-44ea-b316-b355c856e94a",
                                "sense_id": "6091919b-da9b-3c29-affa-f5d16a78ecd5",
                                "text": "They worked from the clinch against the ringposts and Daniel handfought to get the Thai Plum, one hand clasped over the other behind the other man’s neck, and there he pinched his elbows together and ragdolled Jung Woo, stepped wide and flung him across the canvas, pulled him back to where knees could be landed if they’d been thrown."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e922df4-66e5-4269-9a38-0250bf14ff0f",
                                "sense_id": "6091919b-da9b-3c29-affa-f5d16a78ecd5",
                                "text": "The next time we played Milestone, this time at home, Rob got kicked out of the game in the first period for fighting. It wasn’t much of a fight. The guy wasn’t exactly hellfire on skates. Rob and him dropped their gloves, and Rob proceeded to ragdoll the guy. I don’t think the guy even got a punch in."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb4f7929-5733-4a50-b78a-398cb7522db6",
                                "sense_id": "6091919b-da9b-3c29-affa-f5d16a78ecd5",
                                "text": "The storm was brutal. It ragdolled my skinny body and tossed me all over the vessel until it hurled me right at Captain Vex’s cabin door."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
